  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c8035da2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Outliers.** Because every feature is a code restricted to {-1, 0, 1}, classic numeric outliers cannot occur, and the\n",
    "check above confirms no unexpected values. The closer equivalent is **near-constant features**: two features\n",
    "(`right_click` and `iframe`) have one code in over 90% of rows, so they carry little information on their own.\n",
    "(22 features are binary and 8 use all three codes; `redirect` is unusual in using 0/1 rather than -1/1.) I keep them for now (tree models\n",
    "can ignore them and they are cheap), but they are worth revisiting when looking at feature importance in Milestone 3."
   ]
  },
