   "source": [
    "## 7. Baseline results\n",
    "\n",
    "**Baseline:** a majority-class `DummyClassifier`, which ignores the features and always predicts the most common\n",
    "class in the training data. A learned model has to clearly beat this to be worth anything. I also include a\n",
    "*stratified* dummy (random guesses in proportion to the class shares) as a second reference point.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Metrics** (phishing = positive class):\n",
    "- **Recall** – share of phishing sites caught. Main metric, because a missed phishing site is the costliest error.\n",
    "- **Precision** – share of \"phishing\" alarms that are correct (false alarms block legitimate sites).\n",
    "- **F1** – balance of precision and recall.\n",
    "- **ROC-AUC** – how well the model ranks phishing above legitimate, independent of a threshold.\n",
    "- **Accuracy** – reported for context only.\n",
    "\n",
    "Results are the mean and standard deviation over the 5 CV folds on the **training set**. The test set is not used."
   ]
  },
