  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ebd517a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Reading the baseline.** After de-duplication phishing is the (slight) majority, so the majority-class baseline\n",
    "predicts *phishing for every website*. That gives a **perfect recall of 1.0** while being useless: it flags every\n",
    "legitimate site too, so precision is just the phishing share (~0.52) and ROC-AUC is 0.5 (no ranking ability).\n",
    "This is exactly why recall cannot be used on its own; it must be read alongside precision/F1 and ROC-AUC.\n",
    "\n",
    "The bar the learned models must clear is therefore roughly **F1 ≈ 0.68, ROC-AUC = 0.5, accuracy ≈ 0.52**, while\n",
    "keeping recall high."
   ]
  },
