    "## 8. Summary and next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "**Audit summary**\n",
    "- 11,055 rows, 30 integer-coded features (all in {-1, 0, 1}) and a binary target; no missing values or invalid codes.\n",
    "- 47% of rows are exact duplicates; dropping them leaves 5,849 unique rows. A naive split would put many identical\n",
    "  rows in both train and test, so duplicates are removed **before** splitting.\n",
    "- A small number of feature patterns carry both labels (irreducible noise).\n",
    "- After de-duplication the classes are near-balanced (about 52% phishing).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Evaluation design:** stratified 80/20 hold-out (test set untouched until the end) + stratified 5-fold CV on the\n",
    "training set; one-hot preprocessing inside a pipeline.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Baseline:** majority-class dummy – recall 1.0 but F1 ≈ 0.68 and ROC-AUC 0.5.\n",
    "\n",
   ]
